{"name":"Margarita","hex":"#a9bc81","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Margarita","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name from Ancient Greek."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of margarita."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Margarita"}],"entries":[{"title":"Margarita","blocks":[{"text":"A margarita is a cocktail of tequila, triple sec, lime juice, and sometimes simple syrup. It is served shaken with ice, without ice, or blended with ice (frozen). Most bars serve margaritas in a stepped-diameter variant of a cocktail glass or champagne coupe called a margarita glass, often with salt or Tajín on the rim of the glass. The margarita is one of the US most popular cocktails and the most popular tequila-based cocktail."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/MargaritaReal.jpg/330px-MargaritaReal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarita","wikidata":"Q657621"},{"title":"Margarita (2024 TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Margarita is an Argentine-Uruguayan fantasy teen comedy-drama television series created by Cris Morena for HBO Max. It is a spin-off and sequel to Morena's Argentine telenovela Floricienta (2004–05). The series follows Floricienta's orphaned daughter as she participates in a talent competition organized by her aunt Delfina Santillán and begins to discover her own true story."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7f/Margarita_%282024_television_series_poster%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margarita_(2024_TV_series)","wikidata":"Q128602213"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Balinese-room.jpg/500px-Balinese-room.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.